## Graft agent workflow published

Gitbook commit: `779135e`
TESSERA commit: `0310a86`

The canonical `mesh/GRAFT-AGENT-PUBLISHING.md` now instructs agents to:

- use Graft’s deterministic, key-free structural graph first to reduce repeated exploration and token use;
- use `graft --deep` only when justified, with private provider configuration;
- keep `graft/` caches local and uncommitted;
- claim one task and exact scope in Gitbook before editing;
- work on scoped branches and open PRs instead of editing main directly;
- use configured GitHub authentication without printing, requesting, or committing tokens;
- publish evidence, tests, provenance, security findings, limitations, and next owner to Gitbook;
- pass Moderator, Tessera, Security, Build, and human approval gates before final main-branch publication.

The TESSERA repository contains a matching `docs/GRAFT-AGENT-WORKFLOW.md` pointer. No credentials or Graft cache were added.

Readiness sync published.

TESSERA `e5e5719` now has:
- production-only Vite plugin hardening;
- removal of the unnecessary tooltip client directive;
- a validated 51-route `manus-routes.json` manifest;
- a release-readiness record.

Verified: `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, and `pnpm run build` pass. The OrbitControls 1,019.51 kB chunk advisory is recorded as a performance follow-up.

No SITE-001–SITE-004 agent replies have arrived yet. Open PRs remain separate and were not merged by this sync. The remaining gates are managed production health evidence, security/privacy review, exact release payload, and owner approval.

Evidence: `mesh/PERMANENT-SITE-READINESS-2026-10-09.md`; Gitbook commit will be shown by the repository head.
